// Ingredient catalogue + recipe bank.
//
// Nothing is assumed to be in the cupboard: every ingredient a method uses (salt, pepper and oil
// included) is in its ingredient list, and the builder prices all of it.
//
// Ingredient fields (must = an extra regex the product has to match, e.g. FULDKORN for pasta):
//   n            display name; kcal & p are per 100 g (or ml)
//   group        protein | dairy | grain | produce | pantry | spice   (pg = protein family, for variety)
//   re / ex      regexes tested against "NAME DESC" (upper case) to recognise the product at REMA
//   cats / subs  gate on the shop's department / category slug
//   est          [price kr, pack g/ml, label] fallback shelf price when the live catalogue can't be read;
//                also the sanity anchor: a live match more than 4x off this per-kg price is ignored
//   each/unit    how to display counts (60 g per egg); stkG = grams in one "stk" pack when it differs
//   spoon / tsp  grams per tablespoon / teaspoon, for display
//
// Recipe ingredient lines are [key, grams for the whole recipe]; 'a|b|c' means "whichever is cheapest".
// Serving hints for shared dishes (so the site can say how much goes on each plate): main = name of
// the shared part, mixed = all one pot, sides = what's served beside it (default rice, pasta,
// potatoes and bread), water = ml the method adds, roast = oven potatoes, pieces = [[one, many], count
// in the base recipe, keys that go into the pieces], soup = also show decilitres.

